conky-spotify-nowplaying (1.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The heart is read from the Spotify app's own Liked Songs on your
    disk, so it updates within seconds, keeps working while Spotify rate
    limits the widget, and no longer uses the Web API while the app is
    installed.
  * The tray menu has a Lyrics toggle and a Lyrics scrolling choice of
    Autoscroll or Static.
  * Songs with no synced lyrics show their plain lyrics as a block you
    scroll with the mouse wheel.
  * Lyrics are found through LRCLIB's search when its exact lookup fails
    or errors, instead of showing none.
  * A song saved from one listing of an album that Spotify lists twice
    no longer shows as liked on the other listing.
  * A widget restored from the tray reappears at its saved position
    instead of the middle of the screen.
  * The tray icon no longer logs a Gtk-CRITICAL warning on Wayland when
    the panel is slow to start.

 -- mfagerstrom <48690419+mfagerstrom@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:18:49 -0400

conky-spotify-nowplaying (1.3.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The liked-songs index is read slowly in the background, one page of
    50 songs every 15 seconds, and resumes where it stopped after a
    restart or a Spotify rate limit instead of starting over.
  * The widget's backdrop takes the cover's main colour when the most
    common colour is a near-grey, so a cover with a grey sky and a
    coloured subject is no longer tinted grey.

 -- mfagerstrom <48690419+mfagerstrom@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:18:51 -0400

conky-spotify-nowplaying (1.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Lyrics are cached on disk per track, so a song played again shows
    its lyrics at once and without a network lookup. Tracks with no
    synced lyrics are remembered for a week; the cache keeps the 2000
    most recently used tracks.

 -- mfagerstrom <48690419+mfagerstrom@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:33:32 -0400

conky-spotify-nowplaying (1.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Resize the widget by dragging an edge or corner: the sides set its
    width, the top or bottom edge the height of the lyrics. Reset widget
    size in the top-bar menu puts it back.
  * Text scaling submenu in the top-bar menu sizes the text on its own.
  * Always on top toggle in the top-bar menu.
  * The widget starts at its saved position.
  * Lyrics show as many lines as fit and fade at the edges; instrumental
    lines show a musical note.
  * A placeholder cover while Spotify's DJ is talking.

 -- mfagerstrom <48690419+mfagerstrom@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:47:15 -0400

conky-spotify-nowplaying (1.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Minimize and close buttons next to the heart; the top-bar menu and
    opening the app again bring a minimized widget back (also: conky-
    spotify-nowplaying show|hide).
  * The heart is drawn like the new buttons and brightens on hover; it
    shows an outline, not grey, while the like state is unknown.
  * Background colour picks up a small accent colour on mostly grayscale
    covers instead of grey or black.
  * The app is listed once in the app grid (duplicate main category
    removed).

 -- mfagerstrom <48690419+mfagerstrom@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:14:05 -0400

conky-spotify-nowplaying (1.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Top-bar (AppIndicator) icon with the current track, Start at login and Quit.
  * Back off from the Spotify API while rate limited (429 Retry-After).
  * Fewer Spotify API calls: likes every 30 s, Liked Songs rescanned daily.
  * Fix the installed launcher looking for its files in /usr/src.

